; apod_container: the SELinux type for apod pods that talk to a socket on the host (the apod
; broker's, or a per-run ssh-agent's). It's an ordinary container (udica's base template, the
; same as container_t gets from container-selinux) plus one permission: connecting to unix
; sockets served by the user's own (unconfined) processes. Which sockets a pod can reach is still
; limited by what's mounted into it. Those servers run at the plain s0 level (apod does that), so
; the MCS rule that a container may only connect to a peer its categories dominate holds.
;
; Install: apod selinux install (sudo semodule -i this file and udica's base template).
; Pods then run with --security-opt label=type:apod_container.process.
(block apod_container
    (blockinherit container)
    (allow process unconfined_t (unix_stream_socket (connectto)))
    (allow process container_file_t (sock_file (getattr write)))
)
